quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  17,39,"This is from the wisdom that your Lord has revealed to you. And do not set up another god with Allah, lest you should be thrown into Hell, condemned, rejected."
  17,40,"Did your Lord prefer you with sons, while He adopted (for Himself) daughters from among the angels? Indeed, you utter a terrible saying."
  17,41,And We have indeed explained (the facts) in this Qur’an in various ways so that they may accept admonition. But it increases them only in aversion.
  17,42,"Say: ‘If there were (other) gods alongside Him as they claim, then surely they would have been able to seek a path to the Possessor of the Mighty Throne."
  17,43,Glory be to Him. He is greatly exalted above whatever they say!’
  17,44,"The seven heavens glorify Him, the earth, and whoever is in them. And there is not a single thing, but it glorifies His praise. But you do not understand their glorification. Indeed, He is All-Forbearing, All-Forgiving."
  17,45,"And (O Prophet), when you recite the Qur’an, We put a hidden barrier between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter."
  17,46,"And We have placed coverings over their hearts that prevent them from understanding it, and (there is) a heaviness in their ears (that prevents them from listening to it). And when you mention your Lord alone in the Qur’an, they turn their backs in aversion."
  17,47,"We know best what they listen for when they listen to you, and when they have secret talks, when the wrongdoers say: ‘(If you follow him,) you will be following just a bewitched man.’"
  17,48,See how they strike comparisons for you. So they have gone astray and cannot find the (right) way.
  17,49,"And they say: ‘What! When we become bones and dust, shall we surely be raised as a new creation?’"
